 ## Overview
-Relightable 3DGS extends standard 3D Gaussian Splatting by embedding physically-based material properties into each Gaussian, enabling deferred shading and realistic rendering of complex appearances such as reflections, transparency, and glossy surfaces [S1, unofficial][S2]. Unlike standard rasterization which approximates view-dependent colors via spherical harmonics and fails to represent specular reflections or global illumination, this method decomposes outgoing radiance into a BRDF integration that respects material parameters [S1, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from its siblings by treating alpha-blending as a smoothing filter to stabilize optimization while allowing for physically accurate lighting interactions [S1, unofficial].
+Relightable 3DGS extends standard 3D Gaussian Splatting by embedding physically-based material properties into each Gaussian, enabling deferred shading and realistic rendering of complex appearances such as reflections, transparency, and glossy surfaces [S1, unofficial][S2]. Unlike standard rasterization which approximates view-dependent colors via spherical harmonics and fails to represent specular reflections or global illumination, this method decomposes outgoing radiance into a BRDF integration that respects material parameters [S1, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from its siblings by decoupling geometry processing from lighting and material computations, adapting a two-pass deferred pipeline to Gaussian Splatting for efficient rendering of high-frequency, view-dependent effects [S2].
 
